# hui 214+LP grenade detonating ON THE GROUND (14z-70, maintainer-
# corrected rig). THIS is the reported defect; 83c does NOT reproduce it.
#
# WHY 83c IS THE WRONG RIG — the error this file exists to fix. 83c fires
# 214+MP from the 2P start distance, so the bomb REACHES the opponent and
# what the capture shows is the projectile CONNECTING — the flame sits
# exactly where P2 is standing, engulfing him. That on-contact explosion
# measures fine (76 of 84 drawn tile CONTENTS byte-identical to native,
# same pose at the same frame) and it is NOT what the maintainer
# reported. The reported defect is the ground MUSHROOM, which only
# happens when the bomb never touches the opponent.
#
# TWO THINGS ARE REQUIRED, both missing from 83c:
#   1. LP, not MP. Button strength sets the throw arc; LP is the SHORTEST
#      range, so the bomb lands on the ground short of the target.
#   2. MAXIMUM SEPARATION. Both fighters walk BACK to their own corners
#      first (P1 faces right so back = Left; P2 faces left so back =
#      Right) — at 2P start distance even a short arc can reach.
#
# BOTH SIDES POKED: P1 = Huitzil (0x10), P2 = Victor (0x03 on vsav AND
# vsav2 — the wheels differ, so poke both or the legs are different
# matches). Early window only (replay-80 rule).
# POKES="1400:ff8782:10;1450:ff8782:10;1500:ff8782:10;1400:ff8b82:03;1450:ff8b82:03;1500:ff8b82:03"
300-305 sys=C1
420-425 sys=C2
800-803 sys=S1
940-943 sys=S2
1100-1102 p2=R
1160-1162 p2=R
1300-1302 p1=1
1360-1362 p2=1
# ── walk both fighters back to their corners (300 frames each way)
2900-3200 p1=L
2900-3200 p2=R
# ── 214+LP #1 — quarter-circle back + LIGHT punch
3380-3382 p1=D
3383-3385 p1=DL
3386-3388 p1=L1
# ── 214+LP #2, spaced (the seq-D dispatch thunk shifts frame-pinned
# inputs, so a single attempt can be eaten)
3700-3702 p1=D
3703-3705 p1=DL
3706-3708 p1=L1
3900 wait
